  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council, polled Tuesday 15 January 1929. Sixteen candidates were nominated for twelve seats; four withdrew in the North Ward, leaving twelve, who were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 7 and 9 January 1929). Four candidates withdrew in the North Ward on 7 January, leaving the seven named. Returned unopposed."
